WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.300 --> 00:00:02.435
-Welcome back to "Late Night."

00:00:02.435 --> 00:00:03.569
We're here with Richard Kind,
everybody.

00:00:03.569 --> 00:00:05.104
And we were talking about it.

00:00:05.104 --> 00:00:06.472
You've got a lot of projects
coming up.

00:00:06.472 --> 00:00:07.807
It's on Hulu.

00:00:07.807 --> 00:00:09.308
People are telling me
it's fantastic.

00:00:09.308 --> 00:00:11.277
-I hear it's hilarious.
Oh, jeez. Look at me.

00:00:11.277 --> 00:00:12.912
[ Laughter ]

00:00:12.912 --> 00:00:14.714
-This is "History of the World:
Part Two."

00:00:14.714 --> 00:00:18.017
It's a Hulu series based on
the Mel Brooks film.

00:00:18.017 --> 00:00:21.053
-This one is the story of
Jesus,

00:00:21.053 --> 00:00:22.822
John, Paul, George, and Jesus.

00:00:22.822 --> 00:00:24.356
[ Laughter ]

00:00:24.356 --> 00:00:26.025
And yeah, it's hilarious.

00:00:26.025 --> 00:00:28.427
It was hilarious to do.
I hear it's great.

00:00:28.427 --> 00:00:29.762
And I spoke to your brother.
-Yeah.

00:00:29.762 --> 00:00:33.399
-He said it's hilarious.
I can't wait to see it.

00:00:33.399 --> 00:00:35.835
-And this is based on,
obviously,

00:00:35.835 --> 00:00:37.103
the very famous Mel Brooks film.

00:00:37.103 --> 00:00:38.738
Do you know Mel Brooks?

00:00:38.738 --> 00:00:40.406
Is he someone you've been
lucky enough to know?

00:00:40.406 --> 00:00:42.141
-Yeah, I have. There's
a couple of things.

00:00:42.141 --> 00:00:43.810
First of all, at
the Kennedy Center Honors,

00:00:43.810 --> 00:00:46.111
I sang "The Inquisition"
from "History of the World,"

00:00:46.111 --> 00:00:47.313
so that was thrilling.

00:00:47.313 --> 00:00:49.115
And there's Obama up there,

00:00:49.115 --> 00:00:50.917
and I'm performing for
President Obama.

00:00:50.917 --> 00:00:54.620
Then I did "The Producers"
on Broadway,

00:00:54.620 --> 00:00:56.222
and then I did it at
the Hollywood Bowl.

00:00:56.222 --> 00:00:59.492
So when Mel Brooks wrote
his autobiography,

00:00:59.492 --> 00:01:01.561
there's a chapter about me,

00:01:01.561 --> 00:01:03.996
"the very talented but loud
Richard Kind."

00:01:03.996 --> 00:01:05.031
-Oh, wow.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:05.031 --> 00:01:07.133
That's a very kind way --
-It's so lovely.

00:01:07.133 --> 00:01:08.735
-I would say very talented
and loud.

00:01:08.735 --> 00:01:10.170
I wouldn't make it a "but."

00:01:10.170 --> 00:01:11.438
I would say these are two
great things.

00:01:11.438 --> 00:01:14.040
-He might have,
and I will take it.

00:01:14.040 --> 00:01:15.307
He might have.
-Yeah, okay.

00:01:15.307 --> 00:01:16.375
-I thought I memorized it.

00:01:16.375 --> 00:01:18.410
Hold on, hold on.

00:01:18.410 --> 00:01:19.612
Listen to this.

00:01:19.612 --> 00:01:21.814
-They're listening to
everything you're saying.

00:01:21.814 --> 00:01:23.916
[ Laughter ]

00:01:23.916 --> 00:01:27.020
-But this is important.

00:01:27.020 --> 00:01:29.722
Okay, the other week,
about two weeks ago,

00:01:29.722 --> 00:01:31.490
I have COVID,

00:01:31.490 --> 00:01:33.726
and I told your guys,
so I sent the pictures.

00:01:33.726 --> 00:01:36.596
So you'll see.

00:01:36.596 --> 00:01:40.199
I was sitting in my room
in three-day-old pajamas,

00:01:40.199 --> 00:01:43.369
haven't showered, hand down
the pants like Al Bundy.

00:01:43.369 --> 00:01:45.205
[ Laughter ]
Just watching TV.

00:01:45.205 --> 00:01:48.107
It's 4:00, it's probably 1:00
out in L.A.,

00:01:48.107 --> 00:01:50.109
and I get a phone call.

00:01:50.109 --> 00:01:52.578
"Hey, Richard.
Who do you think this is?"

00:01:52.578 --> 00:01:53.646
I don't know.

00:01:53.646 --> 00:01:55.514
Then I go, "Who do you think
this is?"

00:01:55.514 --> 00:01:56.549
I don't know.

00:01:56.549 --> 00:01:58.351
We go to FaceTime.

00:01:58.351 --> 00:02:02.355
I get a phone call --
listen to this.

00:02:02.355 --> 00:02:07.927
Mel Brooks, Norman Lear,
and Dick Van Dyke.

00:02:07.927 --> 00:02:10.229
Mount Rushmore.
-It is Mount Rushmore.

00:02:10.229 --> 00:02:12.431
-Are calling me,
and Judd Apatow,

00:02:12.431 --> 00:02:14.701
who is I guess, FDR.

00:02:14.701 --> 00:02:16.368
[ Laughter ]

00:02:16.368 --> 00:02:19.204
Look at this!
-Look at your face!

00:02:19.204 --> 00:02:21.407
-I know. I couldn't believe it.

00:02:21.407 --> 00:02:23.743
I couldn't believe it.
There's Mel Brooks.

00:02:23.743 --> 00:02:25.478
-And here, by the way,
this is lovely.

00:02:25.478 --> 00:02:27.079
This is all of them in the room,
and they called you.

00:02:27.079 --> 00:02:28.781
Can I just say,

00:02:28.781 --> 00:02:33.252
I am in awe of Dick Van Dyke
and his spryness.

00:02:33.252 --> 00:02:35.387
All of them.
-They're all young and fit,

00:02:35.387 --> 00:02:36.522
and there's all this food.

00:02:36.522 --> 00:02:38.157
I would be like this
the entire time.

00:02:38.157 --> 00:02:39.992
They're all sitting up
and talking,

00:02:39.992 --> 00:02:41.394
which is why they're
thin and healthy.

00:02:41.394 --> 00:02:43.763
But there's Mel Brooks.

00:02:43.763 --> 00:02:44.930
Norman on his phone,

00:02:44.930 --> 00:02:48.434
because Mel probably was
talking about

00:02:48.434 --> 00:02:49.535
"History of the World,"

00:02:49.535 --> 00:02:51.403
or they're gonna do "Producers"
in London

00:02:51.403 --> 00:02:52.705
and my name came up.

00:02:52.705 --> 00:02:56.876
I know Norman as a friend,
and so he probably said,

00:02:56.876 --> 00:02:58.010
"Let's call him."

00:02:58.010 --> 00:02:59.845
And out of the blue.

00:02:59.845 --> 00:03:02.882
It is --

00:03:02.882 --> 00:03:04.016
I'm gonna --

00:03:04.016 --> 00:03:05.184
Don't listen to this,

00:03:05.184 --> 00:03:06.852
'cause I haven't got the words
to describe

00:03:06.852 --> 00:03:12.157
just how honored, touched
that I exist in that world.

00:03:12.157 --> 00:03:15.762
-Those people, and I've been
lucky enough to meet --

00:03:15.762 --> 00:03:17.196
and I've ever met Dick Van Dyke.

00:03:17.196 --> 00:03:20.800
They are so warm and giving,
and they understand the value

00:03:20.800 --> 00:03:23.469
of when they tell you,
"Keep up the good work."

00:03:23.469 --> 00:03:24.904
When it comes from them,
my goodness.

00:03:24.904 --> 00:03:28.340
-Right, well, I have met
Dick Van Dyke before,

00:03:28.340 --> 00:03:29.508
the first time I met him.

00:03:29.508 --> 00:03:33.545
I tried to tell him
the effect he had on me.

00:03:33.545 --> 00:03:35.148
He would not let me talk.

00:03:35.148 --> 00:03:36.916
He would just say,
"You're so good."

00:03:36.916 --> 00:03:38.317
It's like he would stop it.

00:03:38.317 --> 00:03:40.820
He put up an electric fence.
He wouldn't hear the compliment.

00:03:40.820 --> 00:03:43.222
But I've told him since.

00:03:43.222 --> 00:03:45.391
Mel will listen.

00:03:45.391 --> 00:03:49.962
[ Laughter ]

00:03:49.962 --> 00:03:51.931
-What a delight to
have you back.

00:03:51.931 --> 00:03:54.333
I want you to know,
you're one of my legends,

00:03:54.333 --> 00:03:55.634
and it is so lovely
to have you.

00:03:55.634 --> 00:03:56.802
-It's so good to see you!

00:03:56.802 --> 00:03:57.903
-You guys, Richard Kind!

00:03:57.903 --> 00:04:00.873
"East New York,"
Sunday nights on CBS,

00:04:00.873 --> 00:04:02.074
streams on Paramount Plus.

00:04:02.074 --> 00:04:03.209
We'll be right back
with more "Late Night."

